==German==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|werdan}}.  Cognate with Dutch {{term|worden}} and obsolete English verb {{term|worth||to become}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|De-werden.ogg|audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|wird|wurde|geworden|past participle 2=worden|auxiliary=sein}}

# {{auxiliary|with an infinitive|past participle: “[[geworden]]”|lang=de}} [[will]]; to be going (to do something); {{non-gloss definition|forms the future tense}}
#: ''Ich '''werde''' nach Hause gehen.'' - “I will go home.”
# {{auxiliary|with a past participle|past participle: “[[worden]]”|lang=de}} to be (done); {{non-gloss definition|forms the passive voice}}
#: ''Das Buch '''wird''' gerade gelesen.'' - “The book is being read.”
#: ''Er war geschlagen '''worden'''.'' - “He had been beaten.”
# {{intransitive|past participle: “[[geworden]]”}} to [[become]]; to [[get]]; to [[grow]]; to [[turn]]
#: ''Es '''wird''' heißer.'' - “It's getting hotter.”

